	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Performances Pl/Python]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=35335#p35335"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>plpgsql is better for SQL-heavy tasks as it supports plan caching, making it faster for such operations. plpython3u is great for tasks needing <a href="https://syntaxscenarios.com/category/python/" rel="nofollow">Python </a>libraries or complex computations, but it&#039;s slower for SQL since it uses the SPI interface. Choose based on your task needs!</p>]]></content>
